GAID promo film, lemo edition (Dark Tech Keynote) — third-party material in the film and its build

Style and tools
- lemo-opuscar, LemoLab, https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar at 3961ddb3d24d8876e0e2754f7790d66908acee51.
  Code and docs MIT (style prompt styles/dark-keynote/STYLE.md, DIRECTOR.md, TECHNIQUE.md; core/audio/sampler.py and sfx.py
  are imported unchanged from the local asset ~/assets/lemo-opuscar/3961ddb/lib, not copied into this repository).
  No lemo demo film, still or voice track is used in the film. Films made with the library need no credit (README "Licence").

Music samples
- Versilian Community Sample Library (VCSL), Versilian Studios LLC, CC0 1.0, via lemo-opuscar's release pack
  instruments-vcsl.tar (sha256 3ed8f753500e629485e323fc7f883b35aca6a77a1ab04522d1d47037d503f6e1).
  Instruments: glockenspiel, hand_chimes, marimba, mbira, tubular_bells, vibraphone, vibraphone_bowed, vibraphone_hard,
  woodblock, xylophone. Score is original; foley is synthesised in code (lemo core/audio/sfx.py).

